# Cuboards — Supabase database (mandatory binding)

## HARD RULE — which database to use

Any time the task touches **Cuboards** and the **Supabase database** (schema, RLS,
migrations, SQL, Auth settings via SQL, seed data, advisors, types, edge functions tied
to this DB):

| MUST | MUST NOT |
|------|----------|
| MCP namespace **`user-supabase-cuboards`** only | **`user-supabase`** (BizTap / `vsujfqufdyoxfaopqcut`) |
| Project ref **`vnsmgvdmxlrfffehzjpf`** | Any other project ref |
| URL **`https://vnsmgvdmxlrfffehzjpf.supabase.co`** | `vsujfqufdyoxfaopqcut.supabase.co` |
| Credentials from **`cuboards/.env`** | `whatsapp/.env` or BizTap keys |

**Before every** `execute_sql`, `apply_migration`, or other Supabase MCP write: call
`get_project_url` on **`user-supabase-cuboards`** and confirm the host contains
`vnsmgvdmxlrfffehzjpf`. If it does not, **stop** — fix MCP or reload; do not proceed
on the wrong project.

If Andre asks for database work while **cuboards** is the active project (see
`.cursor/active-project.md`), this rule applies even when the chat mention is vague
("run a migration", "add a table", "fix RLS").

